{"id": "DfOZ7Xio1Zn", "title": "Video by vigyan_bhairav__", "description": "Method 3: The Expanded Middle 🌌🔥🕉️\n\nMethod 1: FIND the pause between two breaths.\nMethod 2: REST in that pause.\nMethod 3: let that pause GROW until it opens into who you are.\n\nThe breath is a power, Shakti, always moving: out from the heart, and back in again.\n\nBetween the out-breath and the in-breath there is a middle, madhya. Here the power does not vibrate at all. This is spanda at rest.\n\nAt first, this middle lasts only an instant. With practice, it opens and widens (vikasita), until the breath neither goes out (na vrajet) nor comes in (na vishet).\n\nThen every thought, of the world outside and the feelings within, burns away in the fire of meditation. With nothing left to hold on to, the senses turn back and gaze in wonder at their own source.\n\nThis is the thought-free state, nirvikalpa.\n\nHere, you do not reach Bhairava. You become his very form. ✨\n\n⚠️ As in Method 2, never hold or force the breath. Just keep resting in the pause and let it widen by itself, day by day.\n\n🧘 Try it: rest in the pause between breaths. Don't push it to last longer; just notice whether it feels a little wider than last time. Comment 🕉️ if you felt the stillness grow.\n\n📖 Vigyan Bhairav Tantra, Dharana 3 (verse 26)\n⬅️ New here? Start with Method 1 and Method 2 on my page.\nFollow for one method at a time 🪷\n\n#VigyanBhairavTantra #VigyanBhairav #Bhairava #Bhairavi #Shiva #Shakti #Tantra #KashmirShaivism #Spanda #Nirvikalpa #Madhya #Pranayama #Prana #BreathAwareness #Meditation #Mindfulness #Stillness #InnerPeace #SpiritualAwakening #Consciousness #Yoga #Mahadev #HarHarMahadev #Ukiyoe #WoodblockPrint #MeditationReels #SpiritualReels #ReelsIndia", "channel": "vigyan_bhairav__", "uploader_id": "70392958166", "uploader": "Bhairav", "timestamp": 1793592296, "like_count": 8805, "comment_count": 39, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTM